  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "DSH Product Subagent Console",
      "text": "English · [简体中文](README.zh.md)\n\n[](https://github.com/Jokasa7/dsh-product-subagent-console/actions/workflows/ci.yml)\n[](https://github.com/Jokasa7/dsh-product-subagent-console/releases)\n[](LICENSE)\n\nFrom a reviewable plan to evidence-backed recovery — inside one [DeepSeek Harness](https://github.com/deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness) conversation.\n\nThis is an independent community plugin, not an official DeepSeek Harness component."
    },
    {
      "section": "DSH Product Subagent Console",
      "text": "[Install](#install) · [Try it in 60 seconds](#try-it-in-60-seconds) · [Full product tour](docs/product-tour.md) · [Report an issue](https://github.com/Jokasa7/dsh-product-subagent-console/issues)\n\nDSH Product Subagent Console adds a draggable **Subagents** workbench for designing a multi-Agent run, watching the real child tree, checking what actually happened, and preparing a safe next step."
    },
    {
      "section": "DSH Product Subagent Console",
      "text": "| Mode | What it helps you do |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Live** | See native child sessions and compatible Provider runs as a real parent-child tree. |\n| **Plan** | Turn a goal into editable roles, tasks, dependencies, Providers, tools, checks, and budgets; preflight before approval. |\n| **Deviation** | Map approved tasks to actual attempts, replay the event timeline, and find the first evidence-backed mismatch. |\n| **Recovery** | Preview what would be retried or reused, ask factual run questions, export a redacted Run Capsule, and derive reusable workflow candidates. |"
    },
    {
      "section": "See the workflow",
      "text": "| Design and approve the exact task graph | Follow every real child branch |\n| --- | --- |\n| [](docs/assets/agent-plan-zh.jpg) | [](docs/assets/agent-runtime-zh.jpg) |\n| **Plan** — edit roles, dependencies, execution choices, and limits, then preflight the saved revision. | **Live** — inspect actual tasks, lifecycle states, timing, and child relationships on one canvas. |\n| Match the plan to what ran | Preview a safe recovery path |\n| [](docs/assets/agent-compare-zh.jpg) | [](docs/assets/agent-recovery-zh.jpg) |\n| **Deviation** — replay authoritative events and inspect the plan-to-attempt mapping with its evidence summary. | **Recovery** — see affected versus reusable work before producing a Retry or Fork proposal. |"
    },
    {
      "section": "See the workflow",
      "text": "Screenshots use the Simplified Chinese locale; the plugin follows the active DSH language. Open any image for the full-size view."
    },
    {
      "section": "Good fits",
      "text": "- Parallel code, documentation, or repository review where ownership and dependencies should stay visible.\n- Phased implementation followed by independent verification or synthesis.\n- Diagnosing a run that is stuck, incomplete, unexpectedly branched, or missing evidence.\n- Turning a repeatedly verified workflow into a reusable starting point without auto-running it."
    },
    {
      "section": "Try it in 60 seconds",
      "text": "After enabling the planner tool below, open **Subagents → Plan** and use this read-only example:\n\n> Design a read-only three-Agent workflow. Agent A reads the project positioning from `README.md`; Agent B reads `name` and `version` from `package.json`; Agent C uses only A and B's results to return three facts. Do not modify files. Let me review the plan before execution."
    },
    {
      "section": "Try it in 60 seconds",
      "text": "Generate the plan, review its roles and boundaries, run preflight, approve the exact revision, and confirm execution. Then switch between **Live**, **Deviation**, and **Recovery** to see the same run from three practical angles."
    },
    {
      "section": "Try it in 60 seconds",
      "text": "The screenshots above come from a real DSH browser session. The v0.9 build was verified with 4 successful read-only workflow runs, 15 observed child sessions, 30 test files / 245 tests, and package/install smoke checks. See the [complete product tour](docs/product-tour.md) for guided scenarios and expected results."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "Download the `.tgz` file and `SHA256SUMS.txt` from the matching [GitHub Release](https://github.com/Jokasa7/dsh-product-subagent-console/releases), verify the archive, and install it into your active profile:\n\n```sh\nsha256sum --check SHA256SUMS.txt"
    },
    {
      "section": "DSH Desktop — run in Open DSH Terminal",
      "text": "dsh plugin add ./dsh-product-subagent-console-0.9.0.tgz"
    },
    {
      "section": "Regular Web profile",
      "text": "dsh plugin --profile web add ./dsh-product-subagent-console-0.9.0.tgz\n```\n\nRestart DSH Desktop or the Web profile after installation.\n\nPlans may contain user-entered objectives, responsibilities, task briefs, completion criteria, and resource names. Do not put credentials or private content in those fields; see [Data and Privacy](docs/data-and-privacy.md)."
    },
    {
      "section": "Enable planning and execution",
